flash_size_reduction_options:
All flags below are from src/nimconfig.h (1.4.3) and are set by copying nimconfig.h into your sketch folder (or via -D build flags / arduino-cli build --build-property build.extra_flags). For a PURE CENTRAL (client + scanner, NO server) keep CENTRAL and OBSERVER enabled, disable PERIPHERAL + BROADCASTER, leave EXT_ADV off, and shrink MAX_CONNECTIONS:

  // --- roles: keep central+observer, drop server/advertiser ---
  #define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_ROLE_PERIPHERAL_DISABLED      // -16 kB (server role)
  #define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_ROLE_BROADCASTER_DISABLED     // -5 kB (advertising). NOTE: even with peripheral disabled, broadcaster is auto-enabled unless you disable it too (nimconfig.h:161-167) -> you MUST set both.
  // Do NOT define CENTRAL_DISABLED or OBSERVER_DISABLED (you need both to scan+connect).

  // --- extended advertising: leave UNDEFINED (already off on classic ESP32) ---
  // (do not define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_EXT_ADV; it only compiles on C3/S3/H2 anyway and pulls extra code when set)

  // --- connections / buffers: smallest viable for one scale ---
  #define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_MAX_CONNECTIONS 1             // default 3 -> 1; frees controller RAM & slots
  #define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_MAX_BONDS 1                   // default 3 (scale likely unbonded; can leave default if no bonding)
  #define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_MAX_CCCDS 1                   // default 8
  #define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_ATT_PREFERRED_MTU 23          // default 255; smaller MTU => smaller buffers/RAM (raise only if scale needs >23-byte writes)
  #define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_MSYS1_BLOCK_COUNT 8           // default 12 (only lower if you send small data)
  #define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_ACL_BUF_COUNT 8               // default 12 (optional)

  // --- logging: default is already OFF (LOG_LEVEL 5 = NONE) per nimconfig.h:213-214; set explicitly to be safe ---
  #define CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_LOG_LEVEL 5                   // NONE (saves ~32 kB)
  #define CONFIG_NIMBLE_CPP_LOG_LEVEL 0                  // NONE (saves ~32 kB)
  // Do NOT enable CONFIG_NIMBLE_CPP_ENABLE_RETURN_CODE_TEXT / GAP_EVENT_CODE_TEXT / ADVERTISEMENT_TYPE_TEXT (they add 7 kB/1 kB/250 B).

  // --- timestamps off (saves per-value RAM) ---
  #define CONFIG_NIMBLE_CPP_ATT_VALUE_TIMESTAMP_ENABLED 0

Net effect: peripheral(-16kB)+broadcaster(-5kB)+already-off logs keeps you well under 1.25 MB with WiFi also linked. The biggest single wins are the role disables and the default-off logs; EXT_ADV is irrelevant on classic ESP32 (no code path).

UNVERIFIED/limited: CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_SM_LEGACY (225) and CONFIG_BT_NIMBLE_SM_SC (228) are UNCONDITIONALLY #defined in 1.4.3 — there is NO single nimconfig toggle to drop the security stack, so I cannot claim a flag that removes bonding/SMP code. If the scale needs no pairing this code still compiles in; the only way to shrink it is patching those defines (not a supported user option). Exact .bin size depends on the rest of your app + core 2.0.17 and was NOT measured (no build run).
